# LF in the repository and in the checkout.
#
# Windows' default (`core.autocrlf=true`) converts on checkout and back on commit, which warns on every file an editor
# wrote and turns one edited line into a whole-file diff for anyone whose tools disagree about the ending. The shell is
# TypeScript, Markdown and CSS; none of it needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Assets git should never try to normalise.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
